  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PreRC 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'As researchers study a potential new cancer treatment in the lab and
    in animals, you help organize study documents, track samples, and make sure the
    required approvals are in place so the work stays on track.


    <b>During the
    preclinical research stage, research coordinators decide which patients will
    eventually be eligible for the clinical trial.</b>


    Is this <b>true</b>
    or <b>false</b>?'
  explanation: Research coordinators do not decide which patients will participate
    in a future clinical trial during preclinical research. Patient eligibility decisions
    happen much later, once a clinical trial is designed. At this stage, research
    coordinators focus on organization, documentation, and communication so the research
    can move forward responsibly.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: PreClinical
